{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1550079-reps-for-each-line-but-two-werewolves","id":1550079,"title":"Reps for each line, but two werewolves?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-04-12T14:02:22-07:00","id":1550079,"title":"Reps for each line, but two werewolves?","content":"Bit of a tricky one; me and my group were planning on creating a multi-splat group of monsters so we could eventually go after the Midnight Circus. Given how the book mentions that a player group would need a similar mixture of vampires, werewolves, mages, changelings, and wraiths in order to properly stand against it, we were considering having our party create a monster for each line to fit. However, we've got an issue; two of the group are really wanting to run werewolves, and we aren't too sure on what to do now.<br /> <br /> We were considering having one of the two Garou players be a sort-of cross-splat character, like Abominations for Vampire; problem is, we've already got a vampire character, and a Mage-Werewolf is a bit too reminiscent of Haight to be comfortable. Wasn't entirely sure if there were any Changeling or Wraith crosses with werewolves, either. We were also considering having one of the wolves be a representative for either Mummy or Demon, and have the Wraith or Changeling be an NPC, but we also aren't sure on whether the Garou have any crossover with Mummy or Demon, either; I think there was a plot bit from Mummy about a Garou becoming one, but I can't remember.<br /> <br /> Anyone got any suggestions? We are willing to run a Mage Werewolf if that's not too overpowered, but I'd like to get some advice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27528-just-some-guy","name":"Just Some Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-12T16:49:17-07:00","id":1550082,"title":"","content":"A Mage-Werewolf would probably be one of the most overpowered combinations, to be honest. One of the few vulnerabilities that Mages have is them being squishy if you catch them off-guard or hit them with something they don't have a protective spell to stop. Giving one the innate survivability of a Garou would be a massive power boost, not to mention their other innate advantages.<br /> <br /> I've only taken a brief look at Midnight Circus, so I don't know exactly how important it is to have a representative from every splat. I think some of the issues could be overcome by having members of the group who are &quot;caster types,&quot; using rites, rituals, etc. (perhaps even some custom ones designed by the Storyteller), to address more metaphysical problems like accessing certain realms or defending against unusual powers. But picking a good solution will depend on the particular problem that you're trying to solve.<br /> <br /> If there's a splat with powers you really need, having the Storyteller play them as an NPC might be a good idea. It gives them a character who can, within reason, keep the group 'on the rails,' and it also gives the players a bit more freedom to make characters they want to play instead of choosing for powers that the group needs.<br /> <br /> The Garou have a bit of crossover with Mummy because the lore of Mummy is kind of built around a crossover conflict which included the Silent Striders tribe and some of the Fera.<br /> <br /> Demon has some major issues when it comes to crossover with Werewolf. Not necessarily insurmountable, but it'll require some work that will likely weaken or undermine some of the lore and themes of either gameline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-12T18:24:01-07:00","id":1550085,"title":"","content":"Are you optimizing to do what exactly?<br /> <br /> If I am remembering correctly how mage cooperative spell-casting works in Ascension, you could start spending 5 freebies for Willpower 10, 8 freebies for Arete 3, put your 6 Sphere dots in 2 different spheres that no other character has, and repeat this for all the characters.<br /> <br /> Boom, now all of you can cast everything as a ritual, combine your spheres for effects that none of you could do individually and even high level characters would have issue blocking against. And you could do this without even setting foot in the Midnight Circus.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 10-13-2025, 12:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-12T23:45:40-07:00","id":1550092,"title":"","content":"Two werewolves is not such a bad thing for the Midnight Circus module, mostly because werewolves can specialize in so many different things.<br /> <br /> That said I think the advice to make a group of mixed-splat characters can easily backfire, as most of the splats expect a certain amount of cooperation from others of their own kind; esp. at lower levels. The book's adventure can be pretty punishing because you're probably going to need a very wide range of abilities and a combination of players and their characters that can function well as a unit. Having two werewolves isn't really a deal breaker as long as they're not both Red Talon Ahrouns that basically have very little to offer besides good senses and great combat skills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-13T01:00:17-07:00","id":1550094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Just Some Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1550079-reps-for-each-line-but-two-werewolves#post1550079\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, we've got an issue; two of the group are really wanting to run werewolves, and we aren't too sure on what to do now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let them<br /> Two Garou is not that bad, they could even use VERY limited Pack-tactics and depending of their Auspice may be calm enough<br /> A Theurge and a Philodox are the best for such thing especially if you want to intorduce the other &quot;races&quot; to them; they would be willing to work out a temporary alliance even with a &quot;Leech&quot; or whataver you have in the team. But even an Ahroun could find a commong ground with a combat-oriented vampire<br /> The Tribe is another factor of course, a Glass Walkers have quiet dealings with the Vampires while the Shadow Lord's feud with the Tzimiscle literaly legendary. Depending where they are from the Stargazers are familiar enough of the Beast Courts and have a cold but cordial working relationship with the Kuei-jin and not operate under the &quot;kill on sight&quot; policy<br /> The Fianna and the Fae are tied together in a love/hate relationship and a Silverfang Ivory Priest or a Silent Strider mixes well with a Wraith, the later also makes it easy to work with a Mummy<br /> And you can add other Fera to the mix if you really don't want 2 Garou in the team, quite a few are willing quietly working with 'questionable' races<br /> <br /> But if you really want a cross splat? Actually there are not many.<br /> - Garou cannot awaken. They are already born half spirit, which makes them unable to also take on the human/avatar state of an awakened mage. Samuel is a special case, he was a Kinfolk first who became a Mage then became a Skinwalker with a Rite.<br /> - Wraith of a Garou? Practiculary unheard of but there is a Black Spiral Dancer gift that turn any Garou killed with it into a Wraith that's Fetter is the BSD that killed them called<br /> <b>Grave Claws (Rank 2 Gift, Book of the Wyrm 20th Anniversary Edition):</b> The werewolf's claws and fangs become obsidian daggers, capable of tearing the soul loose from Gaia's cycle and pinning it to the Dark Umbra. Any creature slain by this Gift is guaranteed to leave behind a ghost, which is anchored by dark magic to its killer. Outside of risky Umbral quests, only killing the Black Spiral Dancer who used this Gift can return a victim's soul to Gaia. A Nihilach teaches this Gift.<br /> So technically? With a strange set of circumstances your Garou can become a Wraith but would be a Wraith with an inherent Garou form, not a Wraith-Garou hybrid<br /> - Garou-Changeling? Not really exist, not like how the Vampire have the Kiasyd. A Changeling could look and act like a Werewolf tho' just wouldn't be one. But there are Kinfolk-Changelings<br /> - The Spell of Life on a Garou... may ort may not work. Some account say Werewolves can become Mummies, but once they experience their second death, they become forever trapped in the Underworld as a Wraith. Other simply state the Sepll of Life that replaces the missing/weakes part of your soul with an ancient soulpiece would severe the tie with Gaia. Hard to tell<br /> Wepauwet was an ancient Silent Strider and 100% mummy. After Sutekh's Curse made a deal with the Undying Horus: in return for mummification as one of the Shemsu-Heru, Wepauwet would serve Horus thereafter. He hoped to become a living library of Silent Strider history. After his First Death, Owl itself spoke to Weapuwet, warning him that the death-and-resurrection of the Undying violated Gaia's intentions for the Garou. Wepauwet would return to life but once -- if he died again, he would fall be trapped in the Underworld as a wraith forever.<br /> But he was made with the old Spell of Life... The new one that create an Amenti? Good question<br /> - A Garou technically could become a Kuei-Jin if he somehow ends up in Yomi or make a deal with a Yama King.<br /> <br /> At the end of the day it is YOUR game!<br /> If you want to have a Wraith-Garou? A Mummy Garou? A Mage Garou?<br /> As long as you have fun, go for it!<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 04-13-2025, 04:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-15T13:27:23-07:00","id":1550173,"title":"","content":"I actually think that both the Garou-Changeling and the Garou-Demon are easy to make, although not without some work put on it.<br /> <br /> The problem with Changeling is that Chimeric Reality takes a lot of space while playing it, and it may be hard to juggle a single PC that sees things no one else can, all the time. But once you solve this (either going for it, downplaying Chimerical Reality entirely, or just giving Glamour to everyone, so everyone sees crazy shit all the time), Garou can be Kinain, their equivalent to Kinfolk, and have limited access to Arts and Realms IIRC (I'm without the book to confirm right now). In fact, if you don't need Arts and Realms you can simply Enchant everyone and call it a day.<br /> <br /> Demon has the same problem as Vampire: you're instantly stinking of the Wyrm. But if this isn't a problem for your group, then they can be a demon's Thrall. It's only as bad as you want the demon to be and it gives access to almost any Demon power the demon wants to give them, not only Lore. The best powers imho are the abilities to passively sense any supernatural power within a mile and roll to better identify it, the ability to see through illusions of any kind with a simple roll, and the complete immunity to mind/emotion control (and arguably to mind effects in general).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-15T14:13:45-07:00","id":1550175,"title":"","content":"Just... something to keep in mind. The OP specifically mentioned tackling the Midnight Circus. I don't want to spoil anything if folks are going in without knowing the details of the story in the book, but there are some specific considerations the modify normal approaches to normally antagonistic splats working together, and why you want a group with such a wide array of tools in their tool kit. It's also an earlier book that predates the late 2e/Revised additional splats like KotE and Demon; which means those groups have some advantages because they're not accounted for, but that's not the nicest thing to do to the ST either.<br /> <br /> Like, sure, you can bend or break the books rules for characters dipping into multiple game-lines, but that's not inherently a solution to the problems the scenario presents.<br /> <br /> To pull an example from a different game: if you're in a Shadowrun game, you're probably going to end up in situations where your combat focused characters are going to have to play bodyguards to the hacker(s). You can't blast incoming enemies with guns or magic and hack at the same time. Even if you have a super-awesome build that lets you be a great hacker and a great street samurai, most of the time you're going to be doing one of the two in the moment. Ditching some of the rules designed to do soft niche protection isn't going to change the fundamentals of things like action economy and the importance of different specializations within the crew.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, being open to tossing aside some of the crossover rules can make characters with strong abilities to dip into multiple resources, but you still only have so many starting dots, so many freebies, and so much XP, to cover a much broader base of traits. A Garou-Changeling that's spending time doing bunks for a cantrip isn't tossing down Rage to put enemies in a blender, or activating a Gift/Fetish/etc. Depending on the combination, with enough XP you can probably get over that, but that's not necessarily applicable to what the OP asked about. With enough XP any premade module can get steam rolled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}